.TH BINGUX-SETTINGS 1 "2026-10-28" "Bingux 0.1.0" "Bingux"
.SH NAME
bingux-settings \- settings application for the Bingux desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bingux-settings
.RI [ LOCATION ]
.br
.B bingux-settings \-\-search\-provider
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bingux-settings
opens the Settings window: network, Bluetooth, sound, displays, appearance, the
shell's dock and top bar, power, date and time, keyboard, mouse, accounts and
default applications.
With no argument it opens at the root.
With a
.I LOCATION
it opens that page or subpage, and Back leads to the pages above it.
.PP
Only one Settings window runs.
Starting
.B bingux-settings
with a location while the window is open shows that location in the open window
and exits at once.
.SH LOCATIONS
A location is a URI,
.BI bingux\-settings:// PATH \fR[\fB?\fIQUERY\fR][\fB#\fIROW\fR],
or the bare
.IR PATH .
The path names a page or subpage, the query holds one-off state, and the
fragment names a row to scroll to.
.PP
Pages:
.BR network ,
.BR bluetooth ,
.BR background ,
.BR desktop ,
.BR search ,
.BR display ,
.BR sound ,
.BR power ,
.BR keyboard ,
.BR mouse ,
.BR datetime ,
.BR users ,
.BR applications ,
.BR accessibility ,
.BR about .
Run
.B bingux-settings \-\-help
for the subpages.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the locations the window understands.
.TP
.B \-\-search\-provider
Do not open a window. Serve Settings' search index on the application search
socket until killed, so the desktop search can find settings without Settings
being open.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BINGUX_CONFIG_BIN
The
.BR bingux\-config (1)
program to use instead of the one next to
.B bingux-settings
or on
.BR PATH .
.TP
.B BINGUX_REDUCED_MOTION
Set to
.B 1
to turn off animations.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bingux/bingux.toml
The shell's configuration, edited by Settings and by
.BR bingux\-config (1).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bingux/effects/
Sound effects state and presets (see
.BR bingux\-effects (1)).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/bingux/data-usage.sqlite3
Network data usage recorded by
.BR bingux\-statusd .
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/bingux-settings.sock
Hands a location to the running window.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
when the window closes normally or a location was handed to the running window.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bingux\-config (1),
.BR bingux\-effects (1),
.BR xdg\-open (1)
.PP
Documentation: docs/settings.md in the Bingux source.
